## Rules

- One behavior per test
- Watch each test fail before implementing
- Minimal code to pass — no extra features
- Refactor only after green

## Anchor to the Acceptance Criteria (INV-138)

Acceptance tests derive from the issue's frozen criteria, not from your interpretation —
writing tests from your own reading of the issue is grading your own homework.

- Source of truth: the plan's `## Acceptance Criteria` block (`AC-N:` ids frozen verbatim
  from the issue), never a live re-read of the issue.
- Cite the id in the test title: `it('retries 3 times on 5xx (AC-1)', …)` — the reviewer's
  FIT rubric maps each `AC-N` to the test line that proves it.
- State the mapping in the red commit body: "tests map 1:1 to the acceptance criteria of #NNN".
- A behavior worth implementing that maps to NO criterion means the anchor is incomplete:
  update the plan anchor first (or capture it via `arbiter note`), don't silently widen scope.

## When to Skip TDD

Only with explicit user permission, and a granted skip is recorded, never tacit: note it in
the plan (`tdd: skipped — user permission, <where granted>`) so review and verification see
a decision instead of an omission. "This is simple" is never a reason — simplicity predicts
typing cost, not defect rate.
